<title>FRANCE: Total says operating environment stable.</title>
<headline>Total says operating environment stable.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil company Total said on Wednesday that in early 1997, its operating environment &quot;remained relatively stable with an increase in the dollar versus the franc and sustained oil prices&quot;.</p>
<p>It made the statement as it announced it had increased it 1996 net dividend by 21 percent to 10.50 francs.</p>
<p>It said, however, that over the past few weeks crude prices had deteriorated.</p>
<p>The growth in oil and gas production, it said, was in line with forecasts.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
